{"title":"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_23\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 23</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Pure_Geometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Pure Geometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Using_the_answer_choices,_quickest_and_best_for_competitions)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Using the answer choices, quickest and best for competitions)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(better_visualization)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (better visualization)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Cheese🧀🧀🧀🧀🧀)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Cheese🧀🧀🧀🧀🧀)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Whole_AMC_8,_Chapters_included)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Whole AMC 8, Chapters included)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_(Short)_Solution_by_Euclid_Spark_(ANIMATED!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video (Short) Solution by Euclid Spark (ANIMATED!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_23\">Problem 23</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 23\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Lakshmi has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> round coins of diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> centimeters. She arranges the coins in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> rows on a table top, as shown below, and wraps an elastic band tightly around them. In centimeters, what will be the length of the band?\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2026_amc_8_q23.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/5/52/2026_amc_8_q23.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"450\" height=\"307\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/3/6d30b418fbb1edbe048e706ff0e818e3daeb7130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 2\\pi + 20 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } \\frac{5}{2}\\pi + 20 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 4\\pi + 20 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } \\frac{9}{2}\\pi + 20 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 5\\pi + 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"620\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/1/7515446b1c058da4a731f29d9e106397e6a3fca4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  unitsize(5mm);  draw(circle((2,2),2)); draw(circle((10,2),2)); draw(circle((4,2+sqrt(12)),2)); draw(circle((8,2+sqrt(12)),2));  draw(     arc((2,2),2,270,150)     -- arc((4,2+sqrt(12)),2,150,90)     -- arc((8,2+sqrt(12)),2,90,30)     -- arc((10,2),2,30,-90)     -- cycle,     black+3bp );  fill((2,2) -- arc((2,2),2,270,150) -- cycle,     mediumgray+opacity(0.4)); fill((4,2+sqrt(12)) -- arc((4,2+sqrt(12)),2,150,90) -- cycle,     mediumgray+opacity(0.4)); fill((8,2+sqrt(12)) -- arc((8,2+sqrt(12)),2,90,30) -- cycle,     mediumgray+opacity(0.4)); fill((10,2) -- arc((10,2),2,30,-90) -- cycle,     mediumgray+opacity(0.4));  draw((2,2) -- (4,2+sqrt(12)) -- (8,2+sqrt(12))     -- (10,2) -- (6,2) -- cycle);  draw((2,2) -- arc((2,2),2,270,150) -- cycle); draw((4,2+sqrt(12)) -- arc((4,2+sqrt(12)),2,150,90) -- cycle); draw((8,2+sqrt(12)) -- arc((8,2+sqrt(12)),2,90,30) -- cycle); draw((10,2) -- arc((10,2),2,30,-90) -- cycle);  draw((6,2) -- (6,0));  [/asy]\" width=\"292\" height=\"182\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>In order to find the length of the elastic band, perpendicular lines are added to the figure to divide the band into sections for easier calculation. After the additions, the length of band consist of five identical lines and a full circle, the four shaded areas. The total length is five lines, the diameter of the coins, plus the circumference of a coin, so \\(5d + 4\\pi\\). Finally, the length of the elastic band is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/f/2ff9a045ad7fd1e770f605108affc3054e1bc000.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}4\\pi+20}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"107\" height=\"30\" />\n~TutorJack\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Pure_Geometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Pure_Geometry)\">Solution 2 (Pure Geometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Pure Geometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As shown in the figure above, we just connect some lines and do relations to find the straight parts of the bands (That's easy). Now, we need to find the four curves. The three central circles form a triangle with angle measures <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa0a9949f018e121b2093216dd5db13d3abef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />. Extend the lines of that triangle and draw two perpendicular lines going through the top left circle's center. Then, it becomes obvious the angle measure for the two topmost arcs of the band is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa0a9949f018e121b2093216dd5db13d3abef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, the length of the curve is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cd0741bf9eaceb79e4e2eb0cc525478fbc367ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6} \\cdot \\pi \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 = \\frac{2}{3}\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"132\" height=\"38\" />. There are two of these, giving us a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37564a146ae684555283efdf60cf4399f18c4b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{3}\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"23\" height=\"37\" />. Now, the bottom two. We do the same process and this time find out the measure of the arcs is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3fd424e953ac76b50bf6103875acc049d21d3c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />, meaning the length of the curve is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/9/419b20deeaafa878e8398acfba343cf0e77b45f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot 2 \\cdot \\pi \\cdot 2 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"132\" height=\"38\" />. There are two such curves, and thus the total length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/d/1ed9a4f9ca60909beb51d4e343a4e3ac6973a639.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{3} \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"26\" height=\"38\" />. The total curvature length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/c/eace568efb085ca6cb2c641ec2176ae2143c3aac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{12}{3} \\pi = 4\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"38\" />. The straight parts is just additive to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10c9984413bc4912e50e74900ff81e0aa3e0048f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+8+4+4 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"147\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, the length of the band is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/f/9cff07d53caf028ff56f24e82f9084856a04b710.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{20+4\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"74\" height=\"26\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Using_the_answer_choices.2C_quickest_and_best_for_competitions.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Using_the_answer_choices,_quickest_and_best_for_competitions)\">Solution 3 (Using the answer choices, quickest and best for competitions)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Using the answer choices, quickest and best for competitions)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If you look at the answer choices you will notice that all the constants are the same, meaning that we just have to find the coefficient of pi. To do this we can form an isosceles trapezoid with the centers of the four corner circles.\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/2/232c0de9cbd0ec670185735419bbb2e62af38f5e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]     unitsize(5mm);     draw(circle((2,2),2));     draw(circle((6,2),2));     draw(circle((10,2),2));     draw(circle((4,2+sqrt(12)),2));     draw(circle((8,2+sqrt(12)),2));     draw(arc((2,2),2,270,150) -- arc((4,2+sqrt(12)),2,150,90) .. arc((8,2+sqrt(12)),2,90,30) -- arc((10,2),2,30,-90) .. cycle, black+3bp);          fill((2,2) -- arc((2,2),2,270,150) -- cycle, lightgray+opacity(0.4));     fill((4,2+sqrt(12)) -- arc((4,2+sqrt(12)),2,150,90) -- cycle, lightgray+opacity(0.4));     fill((8,2+sqrt(12)) -- arc((8,2+sqrt(12)),2,90,30) -- cycle, lightgray+opacity(0.4));     fill((10,2) -- arc((10,2),2,30,-90) -- cycle, lightgray+opacity(0.4));      draw((2,2) -- (4,2+sqrt(12)) -- (8,2+sqrt(12)) -- (10,2) -- (6,2) -- cycle);     draw((2,2) -- arc((2,2),2,270,150) -- cycle);     draw((4,2+sqrt(12)) -- arc((4,2+sqrt(12)),2,150,90) -- cycle);     draw((8,2+sqrt(12)) -- arc((8,2+sqrt(12)),2,90,30) -- cycle);     draw((10,2) -- arc((10,2),2,30,-90) -- cycle);     draw((6,2) -- (6,0));  [/asy]\" width=\"292\" height=\"182\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p><br />\nOnce we do this we can split the trapezoid into three equilateral triangles, after doing this we can solve for the curved lengths. The bottom 2 curved lengths are each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3fd424e953ac76b50bf6103875acc049d21d3c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/5/7951a161ace376a692b4620e6c36df078bec9fe1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360-90-90-60=120,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"207\" height=\"17\" /> because this is an isosceles trapezoid the top two angles must be the same, thus they are both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa0a9949f018e121b2093216dd5db13d3abef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/5/3557e41ba5e9a7f6db7875df928225e044d335e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{360-(120+120)}{2}=60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"189\" height=\"40\" /> (We can also solve for this like we did for the bottom two by doing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/f/92fa1adab217606d243ada3ab7f8a87b6f9402c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360-90-90-60-60=60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"233\" height=\"15\" />) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/8/36809b0b16480fb5ecfd221a0c652ba58770e3a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60+60+120+120=360$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"211\" height=\"15\" /> so the total curved part is the same as the circumference of the circle which is diameter times <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/b/0bb2bb96d081e9446fee8ff264871c74f51b23c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"16\" /> which is 4*pi which = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/8/9381ee48449564e0513432f95d86f17747bf3e60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\pi,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" /> so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/f/2ff9a045ad7fd1e770f605108affc3054e1bc000.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}4\\pi+20}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"107\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>PS. For problems like these where a band is wrapped around congruent circles, the curved part is always equal to the circumference of a circle. \n</p><p>~SShreyas\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28better_visualization.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(better_visualization)\">Solution 5 (better visualization)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (better visualization)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2026_amc_8_q23_solution5.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/a3/2026_amc_8_q23_solution5.png/600px-2026_amc_8_q23_solution5.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"333\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/a3/2026_amc_8_q23_solution5.png/900px-2026_amc_8_q23_solution5.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/a/a3/2026_amc_8_q23_solution5.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> fourths of a circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so there is one circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Finding the circumference gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a72a1caa0cb9e0f72f414ebd8180ea676808568f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />, and adding the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />'s created by matching the centers of one circle to another by using the radius property gives (it's always equal if it comes from the center) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/f/2ff9a045ad7fd1e770f605108affc3054e1bc000.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}4\\pi+20}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"107\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>-N.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Cheese.F0.9F.A7.80.F0.9F.A7.80.F0.9F.A7.80.F0.9F.A7.80.F0.9F.A7.80.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Cheese🧀🧀🧀🧀🧀)\">Solution 6 (Cheese🧀🧀🧀🧀🧀)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Cheese🧀🧀🧀🧀🧀)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that the coefficient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4c044326e2e84b768dafef07060bd42b0a5cb21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> because the angles in the trapezoid add to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/9/cf9506d61661a7d046ee93b381ddb704684ffd15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360^\\circ$\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />, the circles are the same size, and the formula for the circumference of a circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/f/e4f68616865f3df95939cb3bf31aa946bb0fc5b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />. The straight bits add to the rational bit and the curved bits add to the irrationals (with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />). Therefore, the coefficient is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a72a1caa0cb9e0f72f414ebd8180ea676808568f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> so the correct answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/f/2ff9a045ad7fd1e770f605108affc3054e1bc000.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}4\\pi+20}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"107\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~jeremyq 🧀\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Whole_AMC_8.2C_Chapters_included.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Whole_AMC_8,_Chapters_included)\">Video Solution (Whole AMC 8, Chapters included)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Whole AMC 8, Chapters included)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/kRBVyDyUYVk\">https://youtu.be/kRBVyDyUYVk</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_.28Short.29_Solution_by_Euclid_Spark_.28ANIMATED.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_(Short)_Solution_by_Euclid_Spark_(ANIMATED!)\">Video (Short) Solution by Euclid Spark (ANIMATED!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video (Short) Solution by Euclid Spark (ANIMATED!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/_ryQwdwe2b4\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/_ryQwdwe2b4</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YJnsl4zjdK8\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YJnsl4zjdK8</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Thinking Feet\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/NysU8ooVt_o\">https://youtu.be/NysU8ooVt_o</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3GmtxMC-W1I&amp;t=2827s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3GmtxMC-W1I&amp;t=2827s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1EWu86rE8b/?spm_id_from=333.1387.upload.video_card.click\">https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1EWu86rE8b/?spm_id_from=333.1387.upload.video_card.click</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\